                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Endless Night is a wave shooter that sets the right mood as soon as you are anchored in the middle of the street.  Gun selection is very limited at this time (semiauto pistol or double barrel shotgun/hand cannon...dual weild).  Graphics are decent, creature animations are above average for many VR shooters I have seen (this is something I hope ALL developers improve on).  Sounds are fitting for the creatures and add a good level of spookiness.  The waves difficulty progression seems balanced to allow the player to adjust and learn the monster movements and weaknesses...then it starts to throw mixed moster waves and it ramps up the adrenaline.  I have not survived enough to see if the location ever moves (there is no movement....you are planted in your VR box so give yourself a little room).  Overall, a fun game that keeps you on your toes until you die...seriously, they just keep coming!",
